---A `StructType` config provides a collection of data values, accessible by ParamTypes.
---
---Each struct contains data where each separate input key is a ParamType and the corresponding output value is a
---ValueType matching that of the given param.
---
---Input keys are unique within the config - the same ParamType cannot exist in the same struct multiple times.
---
---These config types can be found within the `config.Struct` table:
---
---Info: An `StructType` is a Proxy usertype, which means it is safe to copy and store in your scripts. It cannot,
---however, be used with any persistent storage.
---
---Information available within an `StructType` includes:
---@class StructType
---@field id integer (Read-only) The ID of this config type.
---@field configName string (Read-only) The name of this config, i.e. `"BOSS_INSTANCE_STALKER_BOSS"`.
---@field typeName string (Read-only) The type of this config. Will always be `"Struct"`.
---@field params ParamType[] (Read-only) Returns a list of all the ParamTypes stored in this config.
local StructType = {}

---Returns the corresponding output value for the given input ParamType.
---@param param ParamType The input param value.
---@return any # The corresponding output value. Returns `param.defaultValue` if the param is not found in the data structure.
function StructType:GetParamValue(param) end

---Returns whether this config contains output data for the given input ParamType.
---@param param ParamType The input param value.
---@return boolean # Whether a corresponding value exists in this config for ParamType.
function StructType:HasParam(param) end
